    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b4409db_fe8edab4",
        "filename": "meson.options",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T17:42:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This option has no \u0027value:\u0027 and hence defaults to \u0027auto\u0027, so opt_bindings_cxx.allowed() is true by default. However, add_languages(\u0027cpp\u0027) (meson.build:33) and dependency(\u0027nlohmann_json\u0027) (meson.build:102) both default to required: true. As a result, a C-only consumer without a C++ compiler or without nlohmann-json now fails to configure, or falls back to the new nlohmann_json.wrap, which fails with --wrap-mode\u003dnodownload (e.g. a Yocto recipe without nlohmann-json in DEPENDS). How about something like this?\n\n```\nopt_bindings_cxx \u003d get_option(\u0027bindings-cxx\u0027)\nif opt_bindings_cxx.allowed()\n    have_cpp \u003d add_languages(\u0027cpp\u0027, native: false, required: opt_bindings_cxx)\n    nlohmann_json_dep \u003d dependency(\u0027nlohmann_json\u0027, include_type: \u0027system\u0027,\n                                   required: opt_bindings_cxx)\n    opt_bindings_cxx \u003d opt_bindings_cxx.require(\n        have_cpp and nlohmann_json_dep.found())\nendif\n```\n\nAlternatively, default this option to \u0027disabled\u0027. phosphor-logging already passes bindings-cxx\u003denabled.",
      "revId": "34475a6245d217a3cff8be093e8ed0e30b901ae3",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
